{%- comment -%}
  READ THE LABEL — signature feature.
  Put two formulas side by side and compare declared doses. Kapiva publishes
  adjectives ("rich in Omega 7"); this publishes numbers, or admits there aren't any.
{%- endcomment -%}
<nav class="wrap crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
  <a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span class="t-dim">Read the label</span>
</nav>

<section class="sec sec--tight" data-reveal>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="coll__head">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="sec-head__pre">read the</span>
        <h1 class="sec-head__main">Label</h1>
      </div>
      <p class="t-lede">
        Most supplement marketing describes ingredients without ever telling you how
        much of them you get. Pick any two Helbrede formulas and compare what is
        actually declared, active by active. Where a quantity is not stated on the
        pack, this page says so instead of filling the gap.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="cmp" data-compare>
      <div class="cmp__pickers">
        <label class="cmp__pick">
          <span class="t-mono">Formula A</span>
          <select data-cmp="a"></select>
        </label>
        <span class="cmp__vs" aria-hidden="true">vs</span>
        <label class="cmp__pick">
          <span class="t-mono">Formula B</span>
          <select data-cmp="b"></select>
        </label>
      </div>
      <div class="cmp__panels" data-cmp-out></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% render 'catalog-json' %}
{% section 'why-helbrede' %}
